-- title:
--   Drinfeld inertia law at the level field, case q=3
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, $A$ a valuation subring of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ with residue field $\kappa=$ `ResidueField A`, and $F=$ `fieldBar q M'`, the intermediate field of the Laurent series field over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ obtained from `xHFunctionField (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` by coefficient base change, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$.
--
--   **Data and standing hypotheses.** *(Level and guard.)* A prime $q$ with $q=3$; a nonzero $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$; a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$. *(The place above $q$ and the supersingular locus.)* A valuation subring $A$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$ which, by `hW`, consists exactly of the places satisfying the predicate `IsSupersingularPlace q M'`; a distinguished $s\in W$; and `hle`, the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`. *(Constant reduction.)* A datum `R₀ : ConstantReduction A (modularFunctionFieldBar M') (modularFunctionFieldC κ M')`, that is: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` with a surjective residue homomorphism onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, a map `R₀.placeMap` on places, and the axioms of `ConstantReduction` (compatibility with $A$ on constants, preservation of degrees, and computation of orders through `placeMap`); together with `hR₀`: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   *(Field of small constants.)* An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb Q\subseteq\bar{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$, such that $A\cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0\to\bar{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field; and `hκ`: every $a\in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some $c\in k_0$ with $c\in A$. *(Auxiliary primes and the tame parameter in $k_0$.)* A prime $\ell$ with $3\le\ell$, $\ell\neq q$, $\ell\nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0\in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$; an element $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. *(Layer family.)* A type $\iota$, a family $K$ of intermediate fields of $k_0\subseteq\bar{\mathbb Q}$, each finite-dimensional over $k_0$, valuation subrings $A_n$ of $K\,n$ which are the pullbacks of $A$, an index $n_0$ with $K\,n_0\le K\,n$ for all $n$, and cofinality `hKcof`: every finite subset of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ lies in the image of some $K\,n$. *(Tame parameter and tame rigidity.)* An element $\pi_t\in A$ with $\pi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q$, and `htame`: every $\tau$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` with `A.tameCharacter πt τ = 1` fixes $K\,n_0$ pointwise. *(Galois stability of $k_0$.)* `hk₀stab`: every $\mathbb Q$-automorphism $\tau$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ with $x\in A\leftrightarrow\tau x\in A$ for all $x$ maps $k_0$ into itself. *(Base layer.)* An intermediate field $K_b$ of $k_0\subseteq\bar{\mathbb Q}$ with $K_b=\bot$, a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ which is the pullback of $A$, and $\varpi_b\neq 0$ generating the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   The field $F$ is regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0\to\bar{\mathbb Q}\to F$.
--
--   **Quantification over the level field.** The assertion is made for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0\subseteq F$ satisfying four conditions: (F1) $f\in F_0$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $f$ lies in $k_0$; (F2) `IntermediateField.adjoin k₀ (range (algebraMap Q̄ F)) ⊔ F₀ = ⊤`; (F3) $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$) and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; (F4) linear disjointness: for every intermediate field $K'$ of $k_0\subseteq\bar{\mathbb Q}$ finite-dimensional over $k_0$, every $m$, every $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\bar{\mathbb Q}$ and every $a:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to F$ with all $a_i$ in the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, if $c$ is $K'$-linearly independent and $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ then all $a_i=0$.
--
--   **Quantification over the model datum.** The assertion is then made for every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ satisfying the following conjunction. (W1) For $x\in k_0$: $x\in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$. (W2) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring. (W3) Its maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\pi_0$. (W4) *(Specialisation at $s$.)* For every $g\in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose base change to `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in `R₀.integers`, if $g$ has non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ at which `jq` has non-negative order, and if the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, then the image of $g$ in $F$ lies in $F_0$, lies in $W_0$, and for every $c\in k_0$ with $c\in A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals the value `s.evalAt` of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference of the image of $g$ and $c$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$. (W5) *(Level invariance.)* For $\zeta$, $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $f\in F_0$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` also in $F_0$: $f\in W_0$ if and only if its image lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (W6) *(Affine chart, Drinfeld reductions and nodes.)* There exist a subring $B$ of $F$ and an $A_b$-algebra structure `alg` on $B$ such that: the structure map of $B$ over $A_b$ is the inclusion $A_b\subseteq K_b\subseteq\bar{\mathbb Q}\to F$; $B$ is contained in the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_b$, and every element of that join is a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$, $h\neq 0$; $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$; $B/(\varpi_b)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$; the image of $\varpi_b$ in $B$ is prime; $f\in W_0$ if and only if $f\cdot h=g$ for some $g,h\in B$ with $\varpi_b\nmid h$; the image of `jq` in $F$ lies in $B$; and $B$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for all $\zeta$ and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$. Furthermore:
--
--   • *(Hasse element.)* There is $b\in F_0$ lying in $B$ such that $b\notin V$ for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which agrees with $A$ on $k_0$ as in (W1), has the image of $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, contains the image of `jq`, and is such that the value at that image of every monic polynomial over $k_0$ with coefficients in $A$ is a unit of $V$.
--
--   • *(Separation of the other supersingular places.)* For every $s'\in W$ with $s'\neq s$ there is $b\in F_0$ lying in $B$ such that $b\notin V$ for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which agrees with $A$ on $k_0$ and satisfies the clause (W4) with $s$ replaced by $s'$ and $W_0$ by $V$.
--
--   • *(Drinfeld reduction with the level law.)* For every algebra structure of `GaloisField q 2` on $\kappa$, every witness that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, and every $\zeta$, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of `GaloisField q 2` and a ring homomorphism $\rho:B\to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) with: $\#C_s=2\cdot$ `placeWidthChar q M' s` (the $j$-width character at `s.evalAt (jGeomGen κ M')`, which for $q=3$ is $6$ if that value is $0$ and $1$ otherwise, divided by `placeRamificationJ M' s`); $\ker\rho=(\varpi_b)$; $\rho$ composed with the structure map of $A_b$ equals the reduction $A_b\to\kappa$ followed by the structure map; every element of the target is a quotient $\rho g/\rho h$; the image of $\rho$ consists exactly of those elements whose image in [`DrinfeldCurve.drinfeldFunctionField q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L12) lies in the image of `CoordRing q κ`; and, for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathrm{red}_q\gamma,1)\in$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) and $f\in B$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹ f` in $B$, the image under $\rho$ of the latter is `hFunctionFieldAction q κ` at $(\mathrm{red}_q\gamma,1)$ applied to $\rho f$.
--
--   • *(Drinfeld reduction with the level law and the tame inertia law.)* For every ring homomorphism from `GaloisField q 2` to $\kappa$, taken as the algebra structure, and every witness that `CoordRing q κ` is a domain, there is a subgroup $C_s$ with $\#C_s=2\cdot$ `placeWidthChar q M' s` such that for every $\zeta$ there is $\rho:B\to$ `quotField q κ Cs` with the kernel, constants, fraction, image and level-law properties just listed, and in addition some $\eta\in\{1,q\}$ such that for every $\pi\in\bar{\mathbb Q}$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$ and $\pi\in A$, every $\tau$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` mapping $k_0$ into itself, every $\alpha\in$ `(GaloisField q 2)ˣ` whose image in $\kappa$ is `A.tameCharacter π τ`, and every semilinear automorphism $g$ of $F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ equal to [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois (xHFunctionField (q^2*M') (levelH q M')) τ`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54): $B$ is $g$-stable, and for every $d\in(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ whose image in `GaloisField q 2` is $\alpha^{q+1}$, with $(\mathrm{diagOneElem}\,q\,(d^\eta)^{-1},\alpha^{\eta})\in$ `hSubgroup q`, and every $f\in B$ with $g\cdot f\in B$, the image under $\rho$ of $g\cdot f$ is `hFunctionFieldAction q κ` at $((\mathrm{diagOneElem}\,q\,(d^\eta)^{-1},\alpha^{\eta})$ applied to $\rho f$.
--
--   • *(Node package.)* There exist: a witness that `jq` lies in `R₀.integers`; a witness that its $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$; a witness `hJK` that `jqNModC Q̄ q` lies in $F$; an element $a_0\in k_0$ with $a_0\in A$ whose residue satisfies $\mathrm{res}(a_0)^q=$ `s.evalAt` of the $R_0$-residue of `jq`; and a finite set `nodes` of subrings of $F_0$, such that `nodes.card` $=q+1$ and: there is a subring $B_c$ of $F_0$ which is the subring generated by the image of $A\cap k_0$ together with a finite set, contained in every node, and each node $O$ is the localisation of $B_c$ at the elements of $B_c$ that are units of $O$; the level automorphisms permute the nodes (for each $\zeta$, $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $O$ there is $O'$ with $f\in O\leftrightarrow$ `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` $\in O'$ for all relevant $f$), and act transitively on them (for each $\zeta$ and each pair $O,O'$ some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ carries $O$ to $O'$ in this sense); distinct nodes $O\neq O'$ admit an element of both which is a non-unit in $O$ and a unit in $O'$; every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ agreeing with $A$ on $k_0$ and satisfying the clause (W4) with $W_0$ replaced by $V$ either contains $B$ or dominates a node (some $O$ with $O\subseteq V$ and all non-units of $O$ in the maximal ideal of $V$); and, for each node $O$: $O\subseteq W_0$, $O$ is local and Noetherian, for $x\in k_0$ one has $x\in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ lies in $O$, and every $f\in O$ is congruent to some $x\in k_0\cap A$ in the sense that $f-x$ is a non-unit of $O$; and there exist $E_0\ge 1$, a witness that $\pi_0^{E_0}=\varpi_t^{\,2\cdot \mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s}\cdot v$ for some $v\in k_0$ with $v,v^{-1}\in A$, a witness that the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $O$, elements $c_x,c_y\in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, a ring isomorphism from the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` over the adic completion of $A\cap k_0$ with parameter the $E_0$-th power of the image of $\pi_0$ (the quotient of the two-variable power series ring by `uvCrossingIdeal`), and units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of that crossing model, such that $c_xc_y=\pi_0^{E_0}u$ in $O$; the isomorphism carries the image of each $x\in k_0\cap A$ to the corresponding `UVCrossingModel.const`; it carries $c_x$ to $\gamma_U\cdot$ `U` and $c_y$ to $\gamma_V\cdot$ `V`; $c_y$ lies in $W_0$ and in its maximal ideal, while $c_x$, when in $W_0$, is not in its maximal ideal; moreover (Igusa branch) the element `jqNModC Q̄ q` $-\,a_0$ lies in $F_0$ and in $O$, and its image under the isomorphism is $w_V\cdot$ `V`$^e$ for some unit $w_V$ and some $e\ge 1$; moreover there is a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ containing $O$, agreeing with $A$ on $k_0$, a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by the image of $\pi_0$, possessing an element $t$ such that for every polynomial over $k_0$ with all coefficients in $A$, if its value at $t$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ then all its coefficients do, with $c_x$ in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ and $c_y$ not, such that for every $g\in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose base change lies in `R₀.integers` and which has non-negative order wherever `jq` does, the image of $g$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_x$, lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ if and only if the $R_0$-residue of $g$ vanishes, and, if that residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, lies in $O$ and is a non-unit of $O$ after subtracting any $c\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue equals `s.evalAt` of that residue; and such that every node $O'\neq O$ contains an element outside $W_x$; and finally there is a subring $B_x$ of $F_0$ whose elements lie in $B$ and in $O$, all of whose elements have non-negative order at every place of $F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ at which the image of `jq` has non-negative order, such that $O$ is the localisation of $B_x$ at the elements of $B_x$ that are units of $O$, every element of $F_0$ is a quotient of two elements of $B_x$ with non-zero denominator, $B_x$ is the subring generated by the image of $A\cap k_0$ together with a finite set, and there is $b\in B_x$ such that $b\notin V$ for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ agreeing with $A$ on $k_0$, having the image of $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, containing the image of `jq` and making the value at it of every monic polynomial over $k_0$ with coefficients in $A$ a unit, provided some element of $O$ fails to lie in $V$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under these hypotheses, for every field $FSS$ that is an algebra over $\kappa$ and every `RegularProlongation R` of $A$ from $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ to $F$ with residue field $FSS$ — that is, a valuation subring `R.integers` of $F$ with a surjective residue homomorphism onto $FSS$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, inducing $A$ on constants and compatible with the residue map of $A$, and such that every non-zero $f\in F$ has a constant multiple in `R.integers` with non-zero residue — such that $f\in$ `R.integers` if and only if $f\in W_0$ for $f\in F_0$, the following holds.
--
--   For every ring homomorphism from `GaloisField q 2` to $\kappa$, taken as the algebra structure, and every witness that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, there is a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of `GaloisField q 2` with $\#C_s=2\cdot$ `placeWidthChar q M' s` such that for every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` there are $\eta\in\{1,q\}$ and a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e:FSS\xrightarrow{\sim}$ [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) with the two following properties.
--
--   (1) *(Level law.)* For every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, every witness $h_\tau$ that `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` preserves `R.integers`, and every witness that $(\mathrm{red}_q\gamma,1)\in$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), and for all $x\in FSS$: the image in [`DrinfeldCurve.drinfeldFunctionField q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L12) of $e$ applied to `R.resAut (levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹) hτ x` equals [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) at $(\mathrm{red}_q\gamma,1)$ applied to the image of $e(x)$.
--
--   (2) *(Tame inertia law.)* For every $\tau$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ`, every $\alpha\in$ `(GaloisField q 2)ˣ` whose image in $\kappa$ is `A.tameCharacter πt τ`, and every semilinear automorphism $g$ of $F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ equal to [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois (xHFunctionField (q^2*M') (levelH q M')) τ`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54): first, $g\cdot f\in$ `R.integers` if and only if $f\in$ `R.integers`; and second, for every witness $h_{st}$ of this stability and every ring automorphism $\varphi$ of $FSS$ which induces $g$ on residues (that is, `R.residue (g • f) = φ (R.residue f)` for all $f\in$ `R.integers`), for every $d\in(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ whose image in `GaloisField q 2` equals $\alpha^{q+1}$, every witness that $(\mathrm{diagOneElem}\,q\,(d^{\eta})^{-1},\alpha^{\eta})\in$ `hSubgroup q`, and all $x\in FSS$: the image in `drinfeldFunctionField q κ` of $e(\varphi x)$ equals `hFunctionFieldAction q κ` at $(\mathrm{diagOneElem}\,q\,(d^{\eta})^{-1},\alpha^{\eta})$ applied to the image of $e(x)$.
--
--   The hedging by $\eta\in\{1,q\}$, chosen after $C_s$ and $\zeta$ but before $e$, is part of the assertion: the inertia law is obtained only up to the $q$-power twist recorded by $\eta$.
--
--   This is the supersingular-reduction step in the construction of a semistable model of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ over a valuation ring above $q$, in the case $q=3$ at a rigid auxiliary level (a prime $\ell_g\equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$): the residue field of a regular prolongation tracing $W_0$ is identified, as a $\kappa$-algebra, with a Drinfeld quotient field, compatibly with the $\Gamma_0(M')$-level automorphisms and with tame inertia acting through the tame character at the parameter $\pi_t$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_of_eq_three_of_dvd_affineChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_of_eq_three_of_dvd_affineChart), which assembles the supersingular discs, nodes and charts of the model over the field of small constants.
